From d0120e3435ba0119248914d4d0715c3168e79d6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:53:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(front): decline a subscript of [][Next]_v that an
 operator leads back to itself

TLC's SubscriptCollector enters the body of each operator the
subscript applies, as an operator, never computing it, so an operator
that leads back to itself, as `RECURSIVE F(_)`, `F(n) == F(n)` does in
`[][x' = x]_<<x, F(0)>>`, directly, mutually, or through a LET, an
operator argument or an INSTANCE, is entered until TLC's stack
overflows. TLC prints the StackOverflowError and exits 255, whatever
-nowarning says. The front end's collector read it without end and
overflowed the process's stack. It now declines where its reading
nests deeper than any subscript's operators do: an operator TLC enters
only as far as an IF or a function application, which it ignores, or
nested applications that end, read as before. No run of the upstream
conformance suite changes.
